WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.224
What is the most expensive product, and the cheapest?

2
00:00:04.224 --> 00:00:07.268
MAX and MIN answer that in one line.

3
00:00:07.268 --> 00:00:12.595
In this lesson, you will learn to write MAX and MIN measures, show them

4
00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:15.258
in cards, and give them clear titles.

5
00:00:15.258 --> 00:00:16.780
Let's find the extremes!

6
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:23.563
I click New measure and name it Minimum Cost per Box.

7
00:00:23.563 --> 00:00:27.983
Typing MIN, IntelliSense lists matching functions and explains each one.

8
00:00:27.983 --> 00:00:31.520
MIN returns the smallest value in a column.

9
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:39.080
The formula:

10
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:43.920
MIN, open bracket, Product, Cost per box, close bracket. Press Enter.

11
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:54.457
Next, Maximum Cost per Box, with MAX.

12
00:00:54.457 --> 00:00:56.783
MAX returns the largest value.

13
00:00:56.783 --> 00:01:00.040
IntelliSense helps you pick the right column.

14
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.235
I add both measures to cards.

15
00:01:15.235 --> 00:01:19.983
The maximum cost per box is twelve point four one, and the minimum is

16
00:01:19.983 --> 00:01:21.340
two point six five.

17
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.500
I copy a text box title, paste it above each card, and edit the text:

18
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.680
Maximum Cost Per Box, and Minimum Cost per Box.

19
00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.680
Now the page shows a clean row of results:

20
00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.000
COUNTROWS with FILTER, maximum, and minimum.

21
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.320
Each number has a clear label.

22
00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.060
Here is another page with more statistical measures:

23
00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:09.780
total products, total countries, the maximum and minimum, and even text results like Argentina and Venezuela.

24
00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:13.640
MIN and MAX work on text too, alphabetically!

25
00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.098
Great work.

26
00:03:17.098 --> 00:03:20.240
These simple measures answer real questions fast.

